cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  RFI Detection in Synthetic Radio Spectrograms: Baseline vs. Hybrid U-Net
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the original
  U-Net RFI method of Akeret et al. (2017) that the baseline reproduces.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh Raina
    given-names: Ronak
repository-code: "https://github.com/RonakSinghRaina/MP"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Pixel-wise segmentation of radio frequency interference (RFI) in synthetic
  radio-telescope spectrograms. Contains a reproduction harness for the U-Net of
  Akeret et al. (2017) using the authors' unmodified tf_unet package, a hybrid
  architecture combining residual blocks, multiscale anisotropic strip
  convolutions and efficient channel attention, a seeded synthetic dataset
  generator that also emits per-pixel RFI strength maps, and a set of control
  experiments (no-learning baselines and a matched-budget architecture ablation).
keywords:
  - radio frequency interference
  - RFI mitigation
  - radio astronomy
  - semantic segmentation
  - U-Net
  - deep learning
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
